      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(skills): surface skill source shadowing",
        "body": "Closes #100071\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users could have a workspace skill silently replace a same-named plugin, bundled, managed, or agent skill without any visible signal in skill discovery, the CLI, Control UI, or doctor lint.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis keeps the existing documented precedence behavior, but records lower-precedence same-name skill sources as shadow metadata on the active skill. The metadata is surfaced in load-time warnings, `openclaw skills list` / `openclaw skills info`, Control UI skill cards/details, and the skills-readiness doctor lint check. This intentionally does not add a fail-closed `denyShadowing` config surface because that compatibility/security policy still needs maintainer product/security direction.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can now see when an active skill is overriding another skill source and inspect the shadowed paths before deciding whether the override is intentional. Existing intentional overrides continue to work.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current head: `841fa419353e2786e77e819dcd3da0470e6c2adb`.\n- Merge repair: merged latest `upstream/main` (`f6b99012435391f18b701330c7b6f40248e6b61c`) into `codex/100071-skill-shadow`; the conflict in `src/skills/loading/workspace.ts` now preserves main's archived-skill filtering and the PR's shadow metadata recording.\n- Claim proved: same-name lower-precedence skill sources are retained as shadow metadata and surfaced through CLI list/info, Control UI, and doctor lint; archived skills do not participate in the shadow warning path.\n- Current-head light verification: `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` -> passed.\n- Focused local Vitest/oxfmt proof still needs a dependency-ready environment; this Windows worktree has no `node_modules`, so `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ...` stops with `OPENCLAW_MISSING_VITEST` before tests execute.\n- Earlier focused proof remains relevant for the unchanged feature path: `workspace-precedence`, skill discovery status, skills CLI, and doctor-core checks passed on earlier implementation heads; real CLI proof showed `openclaw skills list` and `openclaw skills info` exposing the shadowed managed skill; real doctor proof reported the warning-level shadowing lint; Control UI proof showed the list chip and detail `Shadows:` section in the public proof gist.\n- Warning-only behavior preserved: this repair does not add a fail-closed config or policy surface.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. Codex inspected the relevant skill loading, CLI, doctor, and Control UI paths, resolved the merge conflict, kept the warning-only owner boundary intact, and refreshed this PR body for the current head.",
